    <string name="proxy_action">Optimise %1$s of photos</string>
    <string name="proxy_videos_excluded">Videos are never optimised — a lower-quality clip would fail quietly inside an editor.</string>
    <string name="settings_optimise_explainer">Optimising replaces the copy on this phone with a smaller version — about 2048 pixels on the long edge, roughly a tenth of the size. The photo stays in your gallery and opens normally in every app, and carries a small cloud badge so you can tell which are optimised. The full-quality original stays in OneDrive, untouched.</string>
    <string name="proxy_none_nothing_synced">Nothing to optimise yet. A photo can only be optimised once it is verified in OneDrive — set an album to Sync in Album Modes, then run a sync.</string>
