    <string name="backup_modes_off">%1$d off</string>

    <!-- "Tap" rather than "click": the Android convention, on a device with no pointer. -->
    <string name="albums_filter_hint">Tap to filter by mode</string>
    <!-- Shown when a mode button is tapped and no album is in that mode. -->
    <string name="albums_filter_none">No album is in that mode.</string>
    <string name="backup_all_done">Everything is backed up</string>
    <string name="backup_nothing_selected">No albums switched on</string>
    <!--
        "verified" matters: this is what Gallery Sync has confirmed, not what OneDrive contains.
        After a reinstall the ledger is empty and this reads 0, which would otherwise look like
        the user's whole backup had disappeared.
    -->

    <!--
        Removing local copies. Deliberately NOT called sync: sync means the file stays in the
        gallery, and this is the one operation where it does not. The file is not discarded — it
        goes from two copies to one, and that one is verified in OneDrive — but from the user's
        side it leaves the gallery, so the wording says so rather than implying a tidy move.
        The trash note is not softening: space is genuinely not reclaimed until the user empties
        it, and saying otherwise would be a lie they discover later.
    -->

    <!--
        The whole sentence is a plural, not a plural noun dropped into a fixed template — the verb
        and pronoun have to agree too ("1 file … is … it" vs "8 files … are … them"). Languages
        with more than two plural forms, or with gendered pronouns, break even harder on that.
    -->
    <string name="backup_move_trash_note">Your OneDrive copy is checked first and is never touched. On some phones the local copy goes to your gallery\'s Recently deleted; on others it is removed straight away, so treat this as permanent on the phone.</string>
