    <!-- Archive confirmation dialog -->
    <!--
        An Archive album with nothing left on the phone.
        Was two lines, the second explaining that the mode still stands. Ian cut it to one on
        27 Aug 2026, and the mechanism does not depend on the sentence: the row is still listed
        with a tappable Archive badge, which is what makes the mode discoverable and revokable.
        The prose was belt-and-braces, and it wrapped to four lines in a two-column grid.
    -->
    <string name="album_archived_empty">All files Archived</string>
    <string name="archive_confirm_title">Archive this album?</string>
    <!--
        Says only what actually happens. This promised "older than your archive age" until 25 Aug
        2026, and no such setting exists anywhere in the app — so the sentence described a safeguard
        that gated nothing, in the one dialog that constitutes consent for the most destructive mode
        in the product. Someone reading it would reasonably believe only their older files were at
        stake, when every verified file in the album is eligible at once.

        If an age gate is built later the clause comes back. Until then it must not be implied.
    -->
    <string name="archive_confirm_body">Files in %1$s will leave your gallery and move to OneDrive once they are verified there.\n\nFiles added to this album later are covered by the same choice.\n\nThe verified cloud copy is your guarantee — a local removal cannot be promised as recoverable.</string>
    <string name="archive_confirm_accept">Archive</string>
    <string name="archive_confirm_cancel">Cancel</string>

